IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `kn-nouns`
IMPORT `kn-ch1`

-- Mishnah Kinnim: THE COUNTING CORE of chapter 3 -- how many offerings were certainly valid when a
-- priest who did not ask offered a mixture, and the readings of 3:2's "the majority is valid".
-- Target compiler: main.  This module is what chapter 3 (kn-ch3.l4) and the seat call.
--
-- Two things are kept apart here, because the tractate's hardest unit turns on the difference:
--   THE DEFINITION -- the fewest valid offerings over every way the birds could have been divided
--     between above and below (the worst case: 3:3 says "for I say the sin offering was offered above
--     and the burnt offering below").  Computed by search over every apportionment.
--   THE FORMULA -- Moshe Koppel's reading of 3:2's "the majority", proved by him in "משפט קומבינטורי
--     במסכת קינים", Higayon 2, pp. 96-102 (Reiss n. 29 cites pp. 66-71, which the journal's index gives
--     to another article of Koppel's), and independently by Philip Reiss, Torah u-Madda Journal 9 (2000)
--     58-75: the valid count of each kind is the SMALLEST MAJORITY, the smallest sum of some owners' pairs
--     that is at least half the total.  Neither Koppel text was obtained; the formula is Reiss's, and
--     Koppel's own wording is as Eliyahu Beller reports it (Higayon 5, pp. 155-157).
-- kn-tests.l4 asserts that the definition and the formula agree on every case the sources print, and
-- prove/kn-obligations.l4 has a solver prove it for the Mishnah's own case over every apportionment.
-- GENERATED from tools/kn-majority.l4.in by tools/render.py; edit the template.

§ `Kinnim: counting what a priest who did not ask has offered`

§§ `One obligation`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:2 | חטאת העוף נעשית למטה, וחטאת בהמה למעלה.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:3 | עולת העוף נעשית למעלה, ועולת הבהמה למטה.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:4 | אם שינה בזה ובזה, פסול.
-- An unassigned obligation that owes s sin offerings and b burnt offerings, of whose s + b birds `above`
-- were offered above: a bird above is a valid burnt offering up to b of them, a bird below a valid sin
-- offering up to s of them.  The rest are invalid (1:1: a bird's burnt offering above, its sin offering
-- below).
@ref Kinnim 1:1 with 3:1 (src:mishnah-kinnim-1:2-4)
GIVEN o     IS AN `Unassigned obligation`
      above IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the valid offerings of an obligation with so many of its birds above` o above MEANS
        (min above (o's `burnt offerings owed`))
    PLUS (min ((`the birds owed by the obligation` o) MINUS above) (o's `sin offerings owed`))

GIVEN o IS AN `Unassigned obligation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the birds owed by the obligation` o MEANS o's `sin offerings owed` PLUS o's `burnt offerings owed`

-- The same for a whole nest of `pairs` pairs, in plain numbers.  This is the form a solver reads
-- (prove/kn-obligations.l4): NUMBER in, NUMBER out, no list and no recursion.
@ref Kinnim 1:1 with 3:1 (src:mishnah-kinnim-1:2-4)
GIVEN pairs IS A NUMBER
      above IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` pairs above MEANS
    (min above pairs) PLUS (min ((2 TIMES pairs) MINUS above) pairs)

GIVEN pairs IS A NUMBER
      above IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`so many of a nest's birds could be above` pairs above MEANS
        above AT LEAST 0
    AND above AT MOST (2 TIMES pairs)
    AND (FLOOR above) EQUALS above

§§ `The definition: the worst case over every apportionment`

-- A count larger than any mixture holds, standing for "no such apportionment".
GIVETH A NUMBER
`more than any mixture holds` MEANS 1000000000

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:18 | חצין למעלן וחצין למטן, שתיהן פסול, שאני אומר, חטאת קריבה למעלן ועולה למטן.
-- Half above and half below: both are invalid, for I say the sin offering was offered above and the
-- burnt offering below.  ("שאני אומר": the text's own warrant for counting the worst case.)
-- The fewest valid offerings among unassigned obligations of which `above` birds in all were offered
-- above: every way of sharing the `above` birds among the obligations is tried.  The last obligation
-- takes whatever is left, so no apportionment is counted twice.
@ref Kinnim 3:3 (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:18)
GIVEN obligations IS A LIST OF `Unassigned obligation`
      above       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fewest valid offerings among the obligations` obligations above MEANS
    IF above LESS THAN 0
        THEN `more than any mixture holds`
        ELSE CONSIDER obligations
             WHEN EMPTY THEN IF above EQUALS 0 THEN 0 ELSE `more than any mixture holds`
             WHEN o FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
                 CONSIDER rest
                 WHEN EMPTY THEN
                     IF above AT MOST (`the birds owed by the obligation` o)
                         THEN `the valid offerings of an obligation with so many of its birds above` o above
                         ELSE `more than any mixture holds`
                 WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rs THEN
                     minimum (map (GIVEN a YIELD `one share and the rest` o rest a above) (range 0 (min (`the birds owed by the obligation` o) above)))

GIVEN o     IS AN `Unassigned obligation`
      rest  IS A LIST OF `Unassigned obligation`
      a     IS A NUMBER
      above IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`one share and the rest` o rest a above MEANS
        (`the valid offerings of an obligation with so many of its birds above` o a)
    PLUS (`the fewest valid offerings among the obligations` rest (above MINUS a))

-- With designated birds too: of the designated sin offerings, those put above are invalid; of the
-- designated burnt offerings, those put above are valid.  Every number of each that could be above is
-- tried, and the unassigned obligations take the rest of the birds above.
@ref Kinnim 3:3 (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:18)
GIVEN m     IS A `Mixture`
      above IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fewest offerings certainly valid in the mixture` m above MEANS
    minimum (concat (map (GIVEN xs YIELD `with so many designated sin offerings above` xs) (range 0 (min d above))))
    WHERE
        d MEANS m's `designated sin offerings`
        e MEANS m's `designated burnt offerings`
        `with so many designated sin offerings above` xs MEANS
            map (GIVEN xb YIELD `the valid count when so many of each are above` xs xb) (range 0 (min e (above MINUS xs)))
        `the valid count when so many of each are above` xs xb MEANS
                (d MINUS xs)
            PLUS xb
            PLUS (`the fewest valid offerings among the obligations` (m's `unassigned obligations`) (above MINUS xs MINUS xb))

§§ `The general principle of 3:2, clause by clause`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:12 | זה הכלל, כל מקום שאתה יכול לחלוק את הקנין ולא יהו משל אשה אחת, בין מלמעלן בין מלמטן, מחצה כשר ומחצה פסול.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:13 | כל מקום שאין אתה יכול לחלוק את הקנין עד שיהו משל אשה אחת, בין מלמעלן בין מלמטן, המרובה כשר.
-- This is the general principle: wherever you can divide the nests so that none is of one woman both
-- above and below, half are valid and half invalid.  Wherever you cannot divide the nests without some
-- being of one woman both above and below, the majority is valid.
-- THE FIRST CLAUSE is a question about dividing the owners into two groups of equal size (a partition of
-- the set of nests): can the pairs be split so that each owner's birds all went one way?
@ref Kinnim 3:2, the general principle (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:12-13)
GIVEN counts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      target IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some of the nests together hold exactly` counts target MEANS
    IF target EQUALS 0
        THEN TRUE
        ELSE CONSIDER counts
             WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
             WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
                     `some of the nests together hold exactly` rest target
                  OR (    c AT MOST target
                      AND `some of the nests together hold exactly` rest (target MINUS c))

@ref Kinnim 3:2, the general principle, first clause (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:12)
GIVEN counts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the nests can be divided so that no woman's are both above and below` counts MEANS
        even (sum counts)
    AND `some of the nests together hold exactly` counts ((sum counts) DIVIDED BY 2)

-- THE SECOND CLAUSE, on Koppel's reading (Reiss section 6): the valid count of each kind is the
-- smallest majority, which is the total less the LARGEST MINORITY, the largest sum of some owners' pairs
-- that is not more than half the total.  On a mixture the first clause covers, it is exactly half.
@ref Kinnim 3:2, the general principle, second clause, Koppel and Reiss (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:13)
GIVEN counts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the largest minority of the nests` counts MEANS
    go (FLOOR ((sum counts) DIVIDED BY 2))
    WHERE
        go t MEANS
            IF `some of the nests together hold exactly` counts t
                THEN t
                ELSE go (t MINUS 1)

@ref Kinnim 3:2, the general principle, second clause, Koppel and Reiss (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:13)
GIVEN counts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smallest majority of the nests` counts MEANS
    (sum counts) MINUS (`the largest minority of the nests` counts)

-- KOPPEL'S OWN STATEMENT, as Eliyahu Beller reports it (Higayon 5, pp. 155-157, a response; Koppel's
-- article itself, "משפט קומבינטורי במסכת קינים", Higayon 2, pp. 96-102, was not obtained): divide the
-- women into two groups; the division whose two numbers of nests differ least is "an optimal division";
-- the larger of its two numbers is "the majority".  Computed here independently of the rule above, by
-- trying every sum some of the nests can make; kn-tests.l4 asserts the two give the same number.
@ref Kinnim 3:2, the general principle, second clause, Koppel as reported by Beller (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:13)
GIVEN counts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger side of the most even division of the nests` counts MEANS
    ((sum counts) PLUS `the least difference`) DIVIDED BY 2
    WHERE
        `the least difference` MEANS
            minimum (map (GIVEN s YIELD `the distance between` (sum counts) (2 TIMES s))
                         (filter (GIVEN s YIELD `some of the nests together hold exactly` counts s)
                                 (range 0 (sum counts))))

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the distance between` x y MEANS IF x AT LEAST y THEN x MINUS y ELSE y MINUS x

§§ `The readings of "the majority is valid"`

-- Four readings, each with its own text (NOTES.md, fork F3).  Each answers the valid count of EACH KIND
-- (sin offerings, and as many burnt offerings), when the priest offered half above and half below.
DECLARE `Reading of the majority` IS ONE OF
    -- Moshe Koppel (Higayon 2, pp. 96-102; Seder Kinnim, 1998) and Philip Reiss (2000): any number of
    -- owners; the smallest majority.  Koppel says it is implicit in Tiferet Yisrael (Beller); found also
    -- in R. David of Dubno and Z. H. Yaffe (Reiss n. 29).
    `Koppel and Reiss`
    -- Bartenura on 3:1: the cases are pairs of women (one and two, two and three, ten and a hundred); the
    -- larger woman's number is valid.  Says nothing of three or more owners.  Beller (Higayon 5) argues this
    -- is the plain sense, with Ravad, Rosh and Maimonides, reading "and" as "or".
    Bartenura
    -- Tiferet Yisrael, Yakhin on 3:2: if one woman has more than all the others together, her number;
    -- otherwise the others' number.  Matches his own examples; R. Heller's 1-2-3-4-5 refutes it (Reiss).
    `Tiferet Yisrael`
    -- Maimonides, Pesulei ha-Mukdashin 8:6-7: for two nests, the larger is valid, and that because all
    -- of the larger owner's offerings count (8:7).  Says nothing of the count for three or more owners.
    Maimonides

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:11 | חצין למעלן וחצין למטן, המרובה כשר.
-- Half above and half below: the majority is valid.
@ref Kinnim 3:2 (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:11)
GIVEN counts  IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      reading IS A `Reading of the majority`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the valid offerings of each kind under the reading` counts reading MEANS
    CONSIDER reading
    WHEN `Koppel and Reiss` THEN JUST (`the smallest majority of the nests` counts)
    WHEN Bartenura THEN
        IF (count counts) EQUALS 2 THEN JUST (maximum counts) ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN Maimonides THEN
        IF (count counts) EQUALS 2 THEN JUST (maximum counts) ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `Tiferet Yisrael` THEN
        IF `the nests can be divided so that no woman's are both above and below` counts
            THEN JUST ((sum counts) DIVIDED BY 2)
            ELSE JUST (max (maximum counts) ((sum counts) MINUS (maximum counts)))

-- src:rambam-pesulei-hamukdashin-8:12 | היו שתי החובות הסתומות שנתערבו זו גדולה מזו כגון שהיתה אחת ארבע עופות והשנייה שש אם עשה הכל למעלה או עשה הכל למטה מחצה פסול ומחצה כשר ומטעם שביארנו עשה חציין למטה וחציין למעלה אם אחר ששאל עשה כן המועט כשר ואם מדעתו עשה המרובה כשר:
-- src:rambam-pesulei-hamukdashin-8:13 | הלכה ז
-- src:rambam-pesulei-hamukdashin-8:14 | זה הכלל כל שעשה הכהן מדעתו חציין למעלה וחציין למטה ואי אפשר שלא יהיה משל אחד למעלה ולמטה הרי זה המרובה כשר הואיל ודבר ידוע שמקצת קרבנותיו למעלה ומקצתם למטה יהיו כל קרבנותיו כשרים:
-- Maimonides 8:7: "since it is known that some of his offerings are above and some below, all his
-- offerings are valid".  An owner's birds must be on both sides when she has more pairs than half the
-- total: her 2p birds cannot all fit on one side.  Then, on his reading, all her offerings count, and
-- her obligation is met.  For any other owner he says nothing.
@ref Maimonides, Pesulei ha-Mukdashin 8:6-7 (src:rambam-pesulei-hamukdashin-8:12-14)
GIVEN `her pairs`          IS A NUMBER
      `the others' pairs`  IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`on Maimonides' reading, all of her offerings count` `her pairs` `the others' pairs` MEANS
    IF `her pairs` GREATER THAN (sum `the others' pairs`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
